-- title:
--   Chart values are fixed by the branch swap
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring, let $\pi \in W$, and let $f$ be a one-variable power series over $W$. Form the crossing model $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \pi$ (with $\pi$ viewed as a constant series). On this quotient, `crossingSwap π` is the ring automorphism induced by `uvSwapEquiv`, the renaming automorphism of $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ along the transposition of the two indices $0$ and $1$, which carries the ideal generated by $X_0X_1-\pi$ onto itself. The ring homomorphism `chartHom π` from one-variable power series to the quotient is the composite of substitution of the two-variable series `sAmbient W` for the single variable (legitimate as a substitution by `hasSubst_sAmbient`) with the quotient map `mk π`. The assertion is that every value of this chart homomorphism is fixed by the swap: $\mathtt{crossingSwap}\ \pi\,(\mathtt{chartHom}\ \pi\ f) = \mathtt{chartHom}\ \pi\ f$ for all $f$.
--
--   This records one inclusion of the classical description of the fixed ring of the branch-exchange involution on a crossing local model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$: power series in the symmetric coordinate $u+v$ are invariant. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.range_chartHom_le_fixedSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.range_chartHom_le_fixedSubring), which packages the statement as an inclusion of the image of the chart homomorphism into the fixed subring; the converse inclusion, identifying the whole fixed ring with a one-variable power series ring, is a separate statement.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_crossingSwap_chartHom.lean

